Feature: Add greeting_starts_with_hello library function
  As a maintainer exercising nmg-sdlc against this disposable Python host
  I want a greeting_starts_with_hello library helper
  So that callers can verify the greeting prefix without changing greet or the CLI

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Valid greeting reports the expected prefix
    Given the library is importable
    When greeting_starts_with_hello is called with Ada
    Then it returns the Python bool True
    And the value equals greet Ada startswith Hello comma space

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Existing validation is preserved
    Given the library is importable
    When greeting_starts_with_hello receives invalid names
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank
    And the errors are propagated without wrapping

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Existing public behavior is unchanged
    Given the distribution is installed
    When greet and nmg-smoke are used with Ada
    Then greet returns Hello, Ada
    And the CLI exits 0 and prints Hello, Ada followed by one newline
